**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**How to implement.** S6 prerequisite/closure for 001 §H and §S6: the shared item contracts MUST land here so experiment copying includes item mapping before S7. The item itself, with its dial mapping and its revision history (001 §I: an item has its own `Parameter` values, an optional photo (a kit file) and notes; 'Dial mapping: a rotatable item has a zero and a sign (`DialSign` exists). Experiments record raw dial readings, and the zero is an ordinary parameter'; 'Revisions: an item file carries a revision number and a short value history'; the S7.1 brief). In `Kit.fs`, after `Parameter` (step 214), each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S7.1. (1) `ItemDial` = `DialMounted of DialSign` (the item turns on a dial: a raw reading maps to the physical angle as `sign · (reading − dialZero)`, the rule of `MuellerReconstruction.physicalAngle`) | `FixedMounting` (the item is not read off a dial). `member this.parameterAxes : ItemParameterAxis list` answers, for `DialMounted`, the one axis `dialZero` (`AngleParameter`, 0), and `[]` for `FixedMounting`, so the zero is an ordinary parameter of the item. (2) `ItemRevisionRecord = { revision : ItemRevision; parameters : Parameter list }`, the values an earlier revision held: the short value history (fit runs keep every vector, 001 §I). (3) `Item = { id : ItemId; label : ItemLabel; model : ItemModelInstance; parameters : Parameter list; dial : ItemDial; photoOpt : KitRelativePath option; notes : ItemNotes; revision : ItemRevision; history : ItemRevisionRecord list }`. The photo is a kit-relative path to a kit file (step 123). `history` lists earlier revisions, oldest first. `member this.libraryReferences : EntryReference list` MUST be its model's exact entryReferenceOpt followed by bindingReferenceOpt when present, with duplicate references removed: what the kit snapshots and pins when it records the item (step 219). `member this.tryFindParameter (name : ParameterName) : Parameter option`. Two LPs of one model are two items with independent parameters (001 §I), so an item holds its own `parameters` and never shares them. No other member is added. Tests, in `KitItemTests`, over test-local items written as records: `an item references its model's library version once and finds its parameters by name`: an item over `ItemModelVersionInstance` of `ItemModelIds.circularPolarizerModelId` at version 1 answers exactly that version's `entryReference`; each source, ideal-polarizer and stack item MUST also name its model version once and its bound physics dependency; and `tryFindParameter` answers the parameter named `dialZero` and `None` for `nothing`. `a dial-mounted item publishes its dial zero and a fixed one nothing`: `(DialMounted DialNegative).parameterAxes` is the one `dialZero` axis at 0 and `FixedMounting.parameterAxes` is `[]`.

**Acceptance.** After the item lands, `Item` MUST hold its id, label, model, own parameters, dial, photo, notes, revision and history, `Item.libraryReferences` MUST name its model's version once, and `ItemDial.parameterAxes` MUST publish `dialZero` for a dial-mounted item only; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `an item references its model's library version once and finds its parameters by name` and `a dial-mounted item publishes its dial zero and a fixed one nothing`, the count rising by 2; and build, elevation and the fourteen s22 invariants MUST pass. Every item MUST carry an exact ItemModel version, with source/polarizer/sample references treated only as typed physics dependencies; no direct-preset or direct-sample model bypass is permitted.
